---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="Lampleaf Support"
      description="Help for Lampleaf, an illustrated Bible app for iPhone and iPad."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main id="main">
      <article class="policy tile">
        <h1>Lampleaf support</h1>
        <p>A Bible that opens like one.</p>
        <p>
          Need help? Email
          <a href="mailto:randyventures06@gmail.com?subject=Lampleaf">randyventures06@gmail.com</a>.
          Include your app version (Settings, Version), your iOS version, your device, and what
          happened. Please do not send private notes or payment-card details.
        </p>

        <h2>Change your Bible's colour or binding</h2>
        <p>
          Tap the gear in the reader's toolbar, then Binding. You can change the colour, material,
          page edges, ribbon and the name stamped on the cover at any time. The choice you made when
          you first opened the app is only a starting point.
        </p>

        <h2>Change translation, theme or text size</h2>
        <p>
          Tap the translation button (BSB, KJV or WEB) next to the chapter name, or use Settings.
          Tap Aa for Paper, Sepia or Night and for text size. Text size adds to your iPhone's own
          text size setting.
        </p>

        <h2>Listening</h2>
        <p>
          Narration is being added a chapter at a time. A narrated chapter is narrated in all three
          translations, and the recording always matches the translation on the page. If a chapter
          has no narration yet, the Listen page says so and lists the chapters that do. Sleep can
          stop at the end of the chapter, keep playing into the next narrated chapter, or stop after
          5, 15 or 30 minutes with Plus. Genesis 1 and Psalm 23 narration and stopping at the
          end of a chapter are always free. Other available narration and continuous listening
          unlock during the trial or with Lifetime.
        </p>

        <h2>Free trial and Lifetime</h2>
        <p>
          The optional free trial unlocks Plus for 7 days. Nothing is charged when it ends. Continue
          free, or choose the separate $49.99 USD one-time Lifetime purchase (the App Store displays
          your local price). Reinstalling does not restart the trial. Notes export and verse share
          cards remain free. If a chosen premium binding locks, it stays saved and returns when
          Plus is unlocked again.
        </p>

        <h2>Restore purchases and Family Sharing</h2>
        <p>
          Open Settings in Lampleaf, then tap Restore purchases. Use the Apple Account that made
          the original purchase under iOS Settings, your name, Media &amp; Purchases. Allow an internet
          connection for Apple to verify it, and complete Apple's sign-in if requested. Restoring
          does not charge again or restart an expired trial. If a purchase is awaiting approval,
          Plus unlocks after Apple completes it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Lifetime supports eligible Family Sharing. Check your family's purchase-sharing settings
          and that the purchaser is sharing the eligible purchase, then restore on the family
          member's device. The free trial is not family-shared. Contact support with the product
          and app version if access is still missing; do not send payment-card details or private notes.
        </p>

        <h2>Optional daily reminder</h2>
        <p>
          Enable Daily reminder in Lampleaf Settings and choose a time. Allow notifications when
          iOS asks. The reminder is scheduled locally; nothing is sent to us. To stop it, turn off
          Daily reminder, or disable Lampleaf notifications in iOS Settings.
        </p>

        <h2>The reading plan</h2>
        <p>
          The Beginnings plan is an optional seven-day schedule, not a trial or subscription. It has
          no dates: if you skip a day, it waits where you left off. Start, restart or end it from
          Settings, Reading plan. You can always read anything you like, with or without it.
        </p>

        <h2>Your notes stay on your device</h2>
        <p>
          Notes, highlights and your reading place are stored only on your device; there is no
          account or cloud backup. Export a copy from Settings, Your notes and highlights, as
          plain text or PDF. Deleting the app deletes its local notes, so keep an exported copy
          somewhere you control.
        </p>

        <h2>Reading offline</h2>
        <p>
          The complete Bible, search, pictures and narration are included with the app, so they work
          without a connection.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="https://randyventures.com/lampleaf/privacy/">Privacy policy</a> ·
          <a href="https://randyventures.com/lampleaf/terms/">Terms of Use</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .policy h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .date {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
</style>
